# Cloudflare Pages reads this at the built site's root (Vite copies public/
# straight into dist/) — the equivalent of client/vercel.json's rewrites for
# this host. Order matters: the API rule must come before the catch-all, or
# every /api request would be swallowed by the SPA fallback first.
#
# Status 200 (not 301/302) is what makes this a reverse proxy rather than a
# redirect: the browser's address bar and cookie origin stay this site, which
# is required for the session cookie (SameSite=Lax) to ever be sent — see
# backend/app/api/v1/auth.py's cookie and client/nginx.conf's identical
# arrangement in the container build.
/api/*  https://aipnicmp-api.onrender.com/api/:splat  200

# Single-page app: unknown paths are routes, not missing files.
/*      /index.html  200
